{
 "voiceover": "[conversational] Your Claude chats might be public, and you'd never know.\n\n[serious] Chats you never shared stay yours. But one share click makes a link anyone can open, and public pages can end up in search. Imagine your bank statement or a medical question sitting there.\n\nHere's the quick check. 1: Open Claude, go to Settings, then Privacy, and look at your shared chats. Anything you don't recognise, delete or unshare. 2: Check your artifacts. If you published any, unpublish them or make them private. 3: Open the memory settings, read what Claude remembers about you, and delete anything sensitive.\n\n[whispers] The catch? Deleting a link kills the link, but anyone who already copied the text still has it. [playful] And menus move around, so just look for sharing, privacy and memory.\n\nBe honest, when did you last check your shared links?\n\nSend this to the friend who pastes everything into AI.",
 "title": "YOUR CLAUDE CHATS ARE PUBLIC?",
